<accept> The content explicitly states under the "IL-7 signaling" section: "Administration of IL-7 to mice results in an increase in recent thymic emigrants, increases in B and T cells, and increased recovery of T cells after cyclophosphamide administration or after bone marrow transplantation." This directly matches the information provided, with cyclophosphamide administration or bone marrow transplantation being the "certain medical procedures." </accept>

**********Source Check**********

The claim 'Certain types of cells also produce IL-7.' is supported by the citation.
<accept> The content explicitly states: "IL-7 is a hematopoietic growth factor secreted by stromal cells in the bone marrow and thymus. It is also produced by keratinocytes, follicular dendritic cells, hepatocytes, neurons, and epithelial cells, but is not produced by normal lymphocytes." This directly mentions that "certain types of cells" (keratinocytes, follicular dendritic cells, hepatocytes, neurons, and epithelial cells) also produce IL-7, in addition to stromal cells. </accept>

